# sslip.io resolves "3-236-213-144.sslip.io" to 3.236.213.144 automatically -- a free way
# to get a real, publicly-resolvable hostname (which Let's Encrypt requires for a cert)
# without owning a domain. If the instance's public IP ever changes (e.g. after a stop/
# start without an Elastic IP), this hostname must be updated to match.
